<p>LABOUR FORCE - Employment may receive a boost of between 10,000 and 15,000 from the hiring of Census collectors in August, and so economists said a strongish headline figure should be treated with some caution. If employment rises in line with the median forecast, it will be the fifth straight month of positive jobs growth, but employment will still only be about 20,000 higher than it was at the end of last year.</p>
<p>Generally, economists expect jobs growth will only be enough to match new entrants to the labour market, keeping the unemployment rate around 8.5 percent, and as long as it does it will fuel speculation of a fourth quarter rate cut. This should ensure that this data remains one of the most watched monthly releases until the end of this year. Real strength in employment growth is not expected until well into 1997, reflecting the lag of employment behind the rest of the economy, economists said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
